Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 09:09:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] =?UTF-8?q?[sl-port-610]=20Safari=205.0.5=20loads=20go?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ogle.com=20over=20HTTPS=20=E2=80=94=20runtime=20crash=20cascade?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20fixed?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Milestone: WebKit 610.1.15 on 10.6.8 launches Safari 5.0.5, loads
https://www.google.com (TLS), parses/styles/renders, runs JS (timers,
cookies, focus), and survives the full load-delegate chain.

WTF:
- ThreadingPrimitives.h / posix/ThreadingPOSIX.cpp: out-of-line
  WTF_EXPORT_PRIVATE Mutex()/ThreadCondition() ctors + timedWait(Mutex&,double)
  overload for Safari 5.0.5 ABI (empty bodies; PTHREAD_*_INITIALIZER in-class).
- PlatformHave.h: HAVE_AVASSETREADER off under LEOPARD_WEBKIT (drops dangling
  ImageDecoderAVFObjC refs from the excluded decoder).

WebCore:
- WebCoreResourceHandleAsOperationQueueDelegate.mm: run work synchronously when
  already on main thread — fixes operation-queue main-thread self-deadlock.
- ResourceRequestCocoa.mm: iterate allHTTPHeaderFields allKeys snapshot to avoid
  mutate-while-enumerate hang on 10.6.
- PlatformScreenMac.mm: guard 10.8+ accessibilityDisplayShouldInvertColors with
  respondsToSelector: + category decl for BOOL typecheck on the 10.6 SDK.
- ColorMac.mm: makeRGBAFromNSColor uses colorUsingColorSpaceName:
  NSCalibratedRGBColorSpace (10.6 getRed: rejects NSCustomColorSpace).
- NetworkStorageSessionCocoa.mm: httpCookiesForURL uses sharedHTTPCookieStorage
  for default CF storage; cookiesForURL falls back to basic -cookiesForURL: when
  the 10.9+ partition completionHandler SPI is absent.
- PlatformMac.cmake: compile platform/mac/WebCoreView.m (base NSView/NSScrollView
  _webcore_effectiveFirstResponder categories; fixes JS .focus() crash).
- MediaPlayer.cpp: AVFObjC exclusion guard.

WebKitLegacy:
- WebFrameLoaderClient.h/.mm: m_policyListener WeakObjCPtr -> RetainPtr (10.6
  lacks zeroing-weak runtime; matches 605).
- WebHTMLView.mm: guard FontAttributes::createDictionary() call sites under
  LEOPARD_WEBKIT (FontAttributesCocoa.mm excluded on 10.6).
- WebHistoryItem.mm: reimplement _transientPropertyForKey:/_setTransientProperty:
  forKey: via objc associated objects (Safari 5.0.5 calls these post-load).
